    <tags>deskarcade game games arcade minigames overlay desktop desktop-pet lan multiplayer foss</tags>
    <summary>Mini-games that play on top of your desktop in a transparent overlay.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[Desk Arcade plays small games on top of your windows while a build, a deploy or a coding agent is working, and you
still see everything underneath.

## Features

- **Clicks pass through.** Only the game objects take the mouse; clicks anywhere else go to your windows, and the
  overlay never takes the keyboard.
- **Window tops are platforms.** Balls, bugs, pets and towers sit on the top edges of your windows and ride along
  when you drag one.
- **Play while it builds.** `arcade dotnet test` runs a command as usual, shows it on the scoreboard and chimes when
  it passes or fails. Claude Code hooks show whether Claude is working, done or waiting for you.
- **Over fifty games**: hoops, archery, mini golf, pinball, pool, darts, chess, checkers, Sea Battle, Durak,
  solitaire, falling blocks, a typing race and more, with a computer rival in every one, and a co-worker over the
  local network.
- **At work**: the overlay steps aside for presentations, breaks for your eyes and back, meeting warnings, focus
  blocks, timers and notes.
- Desktop pets, themes, achievements and a daily challenge; English, Uzbek and Russian.
- No account, no telemetry: settings, scores and stats stay on your PC.

## Notes

- This package runs the official per-user installer (`DeskArcade-Setup-<version>-standalone.exe`, .NET runtime
  bundled; the native ARM64 installer on Windows on ARM) silently. It installs for the user who runs choco, into
  `%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\Desk Arcade`, and adds the `arcade` command to that user's PATH.
- Settings and high scores in `%APPDATA%\DeskArcade` are kept on upgrade and on uninstall.
- **Ctrl+Alt+G** shows or hides the overlay after it starts.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/BokhodirUrinboev/DeskArcade/releases/tag/v1.8.5</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
